Subject: SOP Ollama Client Profile

Description: The first local model-provider profile for SOP-RVM, using Ollama for inference while preserving SOP as the independent reflective client and runtime.

& [ProfileIdentity] is the canonical SJS provider-profile decision
  + [specification_uuid] is ec219dc1-8f4a-4012-ad45-fbd18481566c
  + [status] is first_provider_profile_not_SOP_identity
  + [decision] is SOP-RVM is the reflective agent client layer and Ollama is its first local InferenceProvider
  + [portability] is later adapters may target llama.cpp server, OpenAI-compatible providers, or other local and remote inference services

& [LayerBoundary] is the responsibility split
  + [SOP_source] owns articulated semantic programs and libraries
  + [SOP_compiler] owns parsing, resolution, checking, semantic IR, and executable package formation
  + [SOP_RVM] owns state, history, attention, scheduling, validation, review, effects, replay, and provider routing
  + [Ollama] owns model loading, token inference, model-specific thinking behavior, streaming, embeddings, and supported model capabilities
  + [model] proposes interpretations, judgments, relations, response content, and tool calls
  = must: retain memory and authoritative state in SOP-RVM rather than rely on Ollama chat history
  = must: validate model output before changing RuntimeState or committing effects

& [OllamaAdapter] is the provider translation boundary
  + [input] is SOP-RVM ReflectionCallPacket
  + [request_target] is Ollama native chat API or supported OpenAI-compatible API
  + [message_projection] is purpose, subject, pertinent history, evidence, current instruction, constraints, and omissions
  + [structured_output] is JSON Schema describing ProposedJudgment
  + [tool_schema] is allowed effect proposals expressed as callable functions
  + [runtime_options] is model, context, temperature, seed when supported, thinking mode, token limit, streaming, and keep-alive policy
  + [output] is normalized ProposedJudgment plus usage and provider metadata
  + [faults] is unavailable model, context overflow, schema failure, truncation, refusal, tool mismatch, timeout, transport error, and provider error
  = must: hide Ollama-specific request details behind the InferenceProvider interface

& [CapabilityFit] is why Ollama is a practical first adapter
  + [local_API] is a local HTTP interface
  + [chat] is multi-message model inference
  + [structured_outputs] is JSON or JSON Schema constrained response generation
  + [tool_calling] is model-proposed function calls returned for client execution
  + [streaming] is incremental content, thinking, and tool-call events
  + [metrics] is prompt, output, load, and evaluation usage data
  + [compatibility] is partial OpenAI API compatibility
  = conclusion: these capabilities implement provider transport and proposal generation while SOP-RVM supplies the missing reflective agent control plane

& [EffectBoundary] is the safety rule for tools
  + [Ollama_tool_call] is a provider proposal
  + [SOP_effect_proposal] is a normalized uncommitted EffectDeclaration
  + [EffectBroker] is the only component allowed to validate authority and commit the tool
  = must: return tool results to the program as observations
  - never: grant a generated tool call direct execution authority

& [StateBoundary] is protection against client-provider fusion
  + [authoritative_state] is SOP-RVM RuntimeState and append-only traces
  + [provider_context] is a disposable projection for one or more bounded calls
  + [model_thinking_field] is provider output that may assist review but does not replace SOP transition evidence
  = must: permit re-creation of provider context from authoritative state
  - never: require one Ollama conversation buffer to preserve agent identity or reentry

& [MinimumAdapterProof] is the first implementation slice
  + [proof_1] is serialize one ReflectionCallPacket to an Ollama chat request
  + [proof_2] is enforce ProposedJudgment through JSON Schema
  + [proof_3] is normalize provider and usage metadata
  + [proof_4] is reject one malformed response without corrupting RuntimeState
  + [proof_5] is run the same fixture through deterministic mock and Ollama adapters
  + [proof_6] is preserve equivalent runtime transitions within declared nondeterminism bounds
  = must: implement only after the deterministic mock-provider runtime proof

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable provider-profile collection
  + [OCP-001] is make SOP-RVM the client and reflective control layer
  + [OCP-002] is make Ollama a replaceable local inference provider
  + [OCP-003] is translate ReflectionCallPacket into structured Ollama requests
  + [OCP-004] is validate ProposedJudgment before runtime-state mutation
  + [OCP-005] is broker all tool calls as uncommitted effect proposals
  + [OCP-006] is prove equivalent fixture behavior through mock and Ollama adapters

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the Ollama client profile trace
  + [fold_1_subject] is SOP-RVM as the reflective client layer over Ollama inference
  + [fold_2_boundary] is program, state, memory, validation, review, and effects in SOP-RVM; token generation and model hosting in Ollama
  + [fold_3_data_design] is call packet, request, schema, proposal, usage, fault, effect, and transition identity
  + [fold_4_governance] is provider abstraction, externalized state, schema validation, tool brokering, and mock parity
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is mock provider first and Ollama adapter second
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is provider lock-in, chat-history-owned memory, generated tool authority, schema trust, and model-thinking-as-proof
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is profile formed; implementation waits for the deterministic SOP-RVM fixture

